    "result": "The fix is now complete. Let me create a summary document:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `gate` command's action handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` was only accepting the `args` parameter but not the `options` parameter from Commander.js. When a user ran `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js correctly parsed `--ci` as an option, but the action handler wasn't receiving it, so the flag was lost when delegating to `frai-gate`.\n\n### The Fix\nI updated the action handler (line 742 in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`) to:\n\n1. **Accept the `options` parameter**: Changed from `async (args: string[])` to `async (args: string[], options: any)`\n2. **Reconstruct command line arguments**: Added logic to iterate through the options object and build a complete command line with both positional args and options\n3. **Pass reconstructed args to spawned process**: Use the reconstructed `cmdArgs` instead of just `args` when spawning `frai-gate`\n\n### Changes Made\n- Modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-768)\n- Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\nThe compiled output in `packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js` now correctly forwards the `--ci` flag to `frai-gate`, which will create both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` (the specification file)\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the GitHub Actions workflow)",
